# API Layer Rules

## Files This Applies To
- `backend/main.py`
- `backend/models.py`

## FastAPI Setup
```python
from fastapi import FastAPI
from fastapi.middleware.cors import CORSMiddleware

app = FastAPI(title="CashFly API", version="1.0.0")
app.add_middleware(CORSMiddleware, allow_origins=["http://localhost:3000"], 
                   allow_methods=["*"], allow_headers=["*"])
```

## App State Pattern
```python
from fastapi import FastAPI
from contextlib import asynccontextmanager

@asynccontextmanager
async def lifespan(app: FastAPI):
    app.state.dfs = {}          # DataFrames loaded here
    app.state.validated = False
    yield

app = FastAPI(lifespan=lifespan)
```

## Required Routes
```
POST /api/load-data       → LoadDataResponse
GET  /api/health          → HealthResponse
GET  /api/cash-position   → CashPosition
GET  /api/cash-leaks      → CashLeaksResponse
GET  /api/backtest        → BacktestResult
POST /api/generate-email  → EmailDraftResponse
```

## Guard Pattern
Every route except `/api/health` and `/api/load-data` must check:
```python
if not app.state.validated:
    raise HTTPException(status_code=400, detail="Data not loaded. Call /api/load-data first.")
```

## Response Models
Always use Pydantic models — never return raw dicts.
All monetary fields: `float`, suffix `_gbp` in field name.
All date fields: `str` in ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD`.

## Error Handling
```python
@app.exception_handler(Exception)
async def global_handler(request, exc):
    return JSONResponse({"error": str(exc), "type": type(exc).__name__}, status_code=500)
```
Never expose pandas stack traces to the frontend.

## Streaming (Email Generation)
Use `StreamingResponse` for `/api/generate-email`:
```python
from fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse

async def stream_email():
    async with anthropic_client.messages.stream(...) as stream:
        async for text in stream.text_stream:
            yield f"data: {text}\n\n"

return StreamingResponse(stream_email(), media_type="text/event-stream")
```
